## Summary

A caller that edits an existing memory location with the documented `name` parameter receives success, but the location keeps its old name. This occurs with both supported explicit selectors, `id` and `number`. The command applies other edits and supports renaming through the undocumented `rename` key, so callers can work around the failure if they know that key.

## Steps to reproduce

On the pinned baseline, save this test as `crates/engine/tests/marker_name_contract.rs` and run `cargo test -p soundcraft-engine --test marker_name_contract -- --nocapture --test-threads=1`:

```rust
