## Summary

Applying Constant tempo at 90 BPM over a range containing a 140 BPM change succeeds, but the later change remains active inside that range. With no interior change, the requested tempo also continues past the range endpoint. Callers therefore receive a successful result without the bounded constant-tempo edit described by the command parameters.

## Steps to reproduce

On the pinned baseline, add the following integration test as `crates/engine/tests/tempo_constant_range.rs` and run `cargo test -p soundcraft-engine --test tempo_constant_range -- --nocapture --test-threads=1`. The test uses the public command entry point and a default 48 kHz session. Both assertions failed during local verification.

```rust
